## 2. Design System & Theming Mandate: GNOME 50 Adwaita & KDE Breeze Cursors

Every UI element, section, card, button, input, dialog, and widget MUST strictly adhere to the **GNOME 50 Adwaita** design system:

### Visual Aesthetics & Glassmorphism
- **Surfaces**: Use `var(--gnome-surface)` for main surfaces, `var(--gnome-card)` for sub-cards, and `var(--gnome-sidebar)` for sidebars.
- **Glassmorphism**: Use `var(--blur-effect)` or `var(--blur-subtle)` with hairline borders `1px solid var(--gnome-border)` or `var(--gnome-border-subtle)`.
- **Corner Radii Hierarchy**:
  - Windows & top-level containers: `var(--radius-window, 16px)`
  - Inner cards, dialog panels, sub-sections: `var(--radius-card, 12px)`
  - Controls (buttons, inputs, segmented toggles): `var(--radius-control, 8px)`
  - Badges, pills, tags, chips: `var(--radius-pill, 999px)`
- **Interactive Controls**:
  - Buttons: `.button-primary` (accent gradient, top inset highlight, hover lift `translateY(-1px)`), `.button-secondary` (subtle card background, GNOME hover lift).
  - Inputs: `.input-primary` with inset depth shadow and 3px accent focus ring (`0 0 0 3px var(--accent-shadow)`).
  - Never use inline `style="..."` attributes. Apply CSS/SCSS classes exclusively.

### Motion & Physics
- Easing: Use GNOME cubic-bezier `var(--ease-gnome) = cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.8, 0.25, 1)` and spring physics `var(--ease-spring) = cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1)`.
- Transitions: standard `var(--transition-fast, 150ms)`, `var(--transition-normal, 250ms)`.

### KDE Plasma Breeze Cursor Hierarchy
- All interactive elements must use KDE Plasma Breeze cursor tokens:
  - Default: `var(--cursor-default)`
  - Clickables / Buttons: `var(--cursor-pointer)`
  - Text inputs: `var(--cursor-text)`
  - Draggable elements: `var(--cursor-grab)`
  - Active dragging: `var(--cursor-grabbing)`
  - Disabled controls: `var(--cursor-not-allowed)`
  - Async operations & network requests: `var(--cursor-progress)` (23-frame animated engine)

